BRepMesh: the cone seam amplifier swaps a seam's pcurves when they are lines with the slightest slope in U.

Against OCCT 3d097a0328 (8.1). Found 2026-10-25 (CLAUDE.md, "OCCT"); not reported upstream (the user's choice).

BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor's SeamEdgeAmplifier adds points to the seams of cones, splitting the edge and both its
pcurves. It matches the geometric pcurves to the discrete ones by the U of the geometric pcurve's point at
FirstParameter(): for a Geom2d_Line that is -2e100, so a seam line whose direction has any U component (3.35e-14 in
conical-surface.step, from a reference direction written as (0, -1, 1.047e-14)) is evaluated about 1e86 away, never
matches, and the pcurves are always swapped. When they were in the right order, the split seam's points land on the
other side of the face, its boundary crosses itself in UV, and the face is left unmeshed (IMeshData_Failure).
OCCT 7.6 (occt-import-js) meshes the face.

The fix evaluates the pcurve at the start of the edge's range instead.

Check: occt-import-js/test/testfiles/conical-surface/conical-surface.step, cone face #78: 0 triangles without the
patch, meshed with it (packages/tess-occt/test/occt.test.ts). In the corpus it is the only face this patch changes.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx
index 6f637819..b2959364 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKMesh/BRepMesh/BRepMesh_ModelPreProcessor.cxx
@@ -210,21 +210,23 @@ private:
 
     // Define two pcurves of the seam-edge.
     occ::handle<Geom2d_Curve> aPC1, aPC2;
-    double                    af, al;
+    double                    af1, al1, af2, al2;
 
     aE.Orientation(TopAbs_FORWARD);
-    aPC1 = BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface(aE, aF, af, al);
+    aPC1 = BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface(aE, aF, af1, al1);
 
     aE.Orientation(TopAbs_REVERSED);
-    aPC2 = BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface(aE, aF, af, al);
+    aPC2 = BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface(aE, aF, af2, al2);
 
     if (aPC1.IsNull() || aPC2.IsNull())
     {
       return false;
     }
 
-    // Select the correct pcurve of the seam-edge.
-    const gp_Pnt2d& aFPntOfPC1 = aPC1->Value(aPC1->FirstParameter());
+    // Select the correct pcurve of the seam-edge, by its point at the start of the edge's range: the curve's own
+    // first parameter can be infinite (a Geom2d_Line's is -2e100), where a seam line with the slightest slope in U is
+    // far from its seam, and the pcurves would always be swapped.
+    const gp_Pnt2d aFPntOfPC1 = aPC1->Value(af1);
 
     if (std::abs(aLPntOfIPC1.X() - aFPntOfPC1.X()) > Precision::Confusion())
     {
